TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"retry","diagnosis":"Failed the ownership gate conflict-domains because attempt 1 never committed anything: HEAD is still the base revision 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa and all four produced artifacts sit untracked in the worktree, so the driver aborted with \"spec-build-driver: agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\" and the finalMessage capture timed out with no worker outcome envelope. The work product itself looks substantially complete and in-boundary — scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, and tests/test_proxy_tooling.py are all inside the conflict domains [\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\"tests\"], the scripts are syntax-clean, and scripts/run-proxy.sh contains the literal results/receipts/proxy.json path the sole acceptance criterion greps for. The failure is purely that the attempt ended dirty rather than committed. One live boundary hazard explains why a naive \"git add -A\" would fail again: the untracked path results/receipts/proxy.json is a runtime receipt emitted by an actual serve run and is NOT inside any conflict domain, so committing it would make the same conflict-domains gate fail for the opposite reason. Attempt 2 steering: 1) Preserve the three existing in-domain files as they are; re-derive nothing and do not rewrite the scripts wholesale — this is a stateless reconcile over work already present in the lane. 2) Remove the out-of-domain artifact results/receipts/proxy.json from the worktree before committing (it is disposable runtime output that scripts/run-proxy.sh regenerates), so the tree is clean and no commit touches a path outside the domains. Do not add it to .gitignore or any other file, since those paths are also out of domain. 3) Stage exactly scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, and tests/test_proxy_tooling.py — nothing else — and commit on the assigned branch tally-work/flashnext-cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling. Do not push or merge. 4) Before committing, self-check the acceptance criterion locally: bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh. 5) After the commit, verify with git status --porcelain that the tree is empty and with git show --stat that every path in the commit begins with scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, or tests/. 6) Return the final result envelope as the last message so the adapter's finalMessage capture projects instead of timing out. Note for the record, not for fixing here: the receipt from the attempted run recorded status fail with an engine-core OOM during boot and an amdsmi absence in the container. Those are pair-lane and fork-lane concerns outside this task's authorized paths and outside its single acceptance criterion; attempt 2 must not chase them and must not widen scope to make a live serve pass."}
